<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH BREWER 9MO GROSS PROFIT RISES.</title>
<headline>CZECH BREWER 9MO GROSS PROFIT RISES.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for nine months ending September 30, 1996: (in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Gross profit	  281.470     vs	 229.867</p>
<p> Operating profit	  n/a     vs	 243.527</p>
<p>Sales of own goods</p>
<p> and services	1,188.641     vs     1,014.002</p>
<p> Total assets	3,971.371     vs     2,622.451</p>
<p> Basic capital	     n/a     vs	 792.911</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Pivovar Radegast a.s., one of the largest Czech brewers. Britain's Bass plc holds 19.96 percent in the firm. Radegast shares are listed on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange. The figures, provided by the company, did not include operating profit and basic capital data.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
